{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nt3fDEkz8acAdSnE3fumsQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a complete picture. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found how zerocheck Round 0 rules are precomputed at keygen time. Here are the key details:\n\n### 1. **AirDataGpu Structure** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`, lines 24-36)\n\n`AirDataGpu` stores:\n- `zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>` (line 28) — the encoded rules for Round 0 zerocheck constraints\n- `logup_round0_buffer_size: u32` (line 35) — pre-computed buffer size for logup Round 0 interaction evaluation DAG\n\n### 2. **SymbolicRulesOnDevice Type** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/rules/mod.rs`, lines 98-106)\n\n`SymbolicRulesGpu<F>` (not `SymbolicRulesOnDevice`) is the stored type. It contains:\n- `rules: Vec<RuleWithFlag<F>>` — vector of three-address code rules\n- `buffer_size: usize` — intermediate buffer size required for evaluation\n- `dag_idx_to_rule_idx: FxHashMap<usize, usize>` — mapping for accumulated constraint nodes\n\n### 3. **Keygen Construction Path** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`, lines 89-152)\n\n`AirDataGpu::new(pk)` (called from `data_transporter.rs:48` during proving key transport):\n1. **For zerocheck_round0** (lines 96, 324-354): `ConstraintOnlyRules::<true>::new(&dag.constraints)` builds encoded rules using `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` with `buffer_vars=true`\n2. **For logup_round0_buffer_size** (lines 113-142): Mirrors the interaction DAG construction, building a fresh `SymbolicDagBuilder`, collecting count and message field expressions, then calling `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)` to extract only `buffer_size`\n\n### 4. **Rule Encoding** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`, lines 307-314, 340-351)\n\nRules are encoded to GPU format:\n- `encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec()`\n- Uploaded via `d_rules = encoded_rules.to_device()?`\n- Along with `d_used_nodes` (constraint evaluation order) and buffer metadata\n\n**Pattern for logup_round0**: Same keygen-time pre-computation approach — build the symbolic DAG at `AirDataGpu::new()` and extract both rules and buffer_size before proving starts."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"418559aa-595d-46f9-bff0-353258f08904","uuid":"fc1b2041-541c-450e-8827-dcff91eceaf7","timestamp":"2026-04-15T15:11:52.667Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand how zerocheck Round 0 rules are precomputed at keygen time in the cuda-backend, so I can do the same for logup interaction rules.\n\nSpecifically, find:\n1. How `AirDataGpu` stores `zerocheck_round0` rules (look at `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs` for the struct definition)\n2. How `logup_round0_buffer_size` is computed and stored\n3. Where `AirDataGpu` / keygen data is constructed — the function that builds the proving key data and uploads rules to GPU\n4. What `SymbolicRulesOnDevice` looks like (the stored type for zerocheck rules)\n\nSearch in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/` with thoroughness \"medium\".\n\nReport: file paths, line numbers, struct fields, and the keygen-time construction code path. Under 300 words.","agentId":"aba789f2c826ae316","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a complete picture. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found how zerocheck Round 0 rules are precomputed at keygen time. Here are the key details:\n\n### 1. **AirDataGpu Structure** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`, lines 24-36)\n\n`AirDataGpu` stores:\n- `zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>` (line 28) — the encoded rules for Round 0 zerocheck constraints\n- `logup_round0_buffer_size: u32` (line 35) — pre-computed buffer size for logup Round 0 interaction evaluation DAG\n\n### 2. **SymbolicRulesOnDevice Type** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/rules/mod.rs`, lines 98-106)\n\n`SymbolicRulesGpu<F>` (not `SymbolicRulesOnDevice`) is the stored type. It contains:\n- `rules: Vec<RuleWithFlag<F>>` — vector of three-address code rules\n- `buffer_size: usize` — intermediate buffer size required for evaluation\n- `dag_idx_to_rule_idx: FxHashMap<usize, usize>` — mapping for accumulated constraint nodes\n\n### 3. **Keygen Construction Path** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`, lines 89-152)\n\n`AirDataGpu::new(pk)` (called from `data_transporter.rs:48` during proving key transport):\n1. **For zerocheck_round0** (lines 96, 324-354): `ConstraintOnlyRules::<true>::new(&dag.constraints)` builds encoded rules using `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` with `buffer_vars=true`\n2. **For logup_round0_buffer_size** (lines 113-142): Mirrors the interaction DAG construction, building a fresh `SymbolicDagBuilder`, collecting count and message field expressions, then calling `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)` to extract only `buffer_size`\n\n### 4. **Rule Encoding** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`, lines 307-314, 340-351)\n\nRules are encoded to GPU format:\n- `encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec()`\n- Uploaded via `d_rules = encoded_rules.to_device()?`\n- Along with `d_used_nodes` (constraint evaluation order) and buffer metadata\n\n**Pattern for logup_round0**: Same keygen-time pre-computation approach — build the symbolic DAG at `AirDataGpu::new()` and extract both rules and buffer_size before proving starts."}],"totalDurationMs":26386,"totalTokens":29360,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1532,"cache_read_input_tokens":27098,"output_tokens":724,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1532},"infere