re, the DAG construction was heavy but the rules upload was already included. After, we skip DAG construction but the weight computation + 2 H2D should be faster, not slower.\n\nHmm, maybe the issue is that before, the DAG construction was overlapping with GPU kernel execution in the multi-threaded Phase 2. The CPU-side DAG work kept the CPU busy while the GPU was processing the previous AIR's kernels. Now with the DAG work removed, the CPU finishes faster and issues the next kernel launch sooner, but the GPU is still busy, so we're synchronizing more on the GPU side.\n\nActually, that doesn't make sense. More available CPU time should be better, not worse.\n\nLet me examine the STARK excl trace more carefully. Before it was 1111ms, after it's 1160ms — that's +49ms. But Round 0 is only +33ms, so there's +16ms unaccounted for elsewhere.\n\nI need to get the full breakdown to understand where the rest of the regression is coming from.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":133430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"418559aa-595d-46f9-bff0-353258f08904","uuid":"a1efbfaa-ca73-44f3-b9bf-80b329565580"}
